pages":[{"id":"generator","label":"seq2seq models"},{"id":"retriever","label":"retriever"}]}],"mentions":[{"citationId":"c38"},{"citationId":"c39"},{"citationId":"c40"},{"citationId":"c1"},{"citationId":"c41"},{"citationId":"c42"},{"citationId":"c43"},{"citationId":"c44"},{"citationId":"c45"},{"citationId":"c46"}],"mentionsLeftOut":146,"citations":[{"id":"c1","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_51dfc9baf42b165f","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":4,"quote":"It incorporates diverse strategies for improving its components, such as adding a search module for similarity searches and refining the retriever through fine-tuning."},{"id":"c2","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_0178f8d07a48f05b","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":52,"quote":"directly influences the GraphRAG system as a whole. Evaluating each component, such as Graph Construction, Retriever, Organizer, and Generator, requires specific designs suited to their unique roles."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_8bf24531e63f4ab4","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":17,"quote":"s We have conducted a comprehensive review of the primary techniques applied in the initial four model-centric components of GraphRAG—namely, the query processor, retriever, organizer, and generator."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_2fc1280370fb0b55","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":7,"quote":"Retrieval Ablations A key feature of RAG is learning to retrieve relevant information for the task. To assess the effectiveness of the retrieval mechanism, we run ablations where we freeze the retriever during training."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_57dcd28abf6833fc","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":9,"quote":"REPLUG [72] utilizes a retriever and an LLM to calculate the probability distributions of the retrieved documents and then performs supervised training by computing the KL divergence."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031_c_976957df22b5c100","docId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031","docTitle":"2401.15884_Corrective_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":3,"quote":"The retriever R aims to retrieve the top-K documents D = {dr1, ..., drk} that are relevant to the input X from the corpus C. Based on the input X and the retrieved results D, the generator G is responsible for generating the output Y."},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_682f79d20bd7bb96","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":3,"quote":"This retriever was trained to retrieve documents which contain answers to TriviaQA [24] questions and Natural Questions [29]."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_5ca9edc552f3ed5e","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":50,"quote":"Balancing retrieved content’s accuracy, diversity, and novelty remains an open-ended challenge. • Reasoning, planning, and thinking along the way: A real-world retriever may need to dynami- cally and adaptively update its retrieve"},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_b987b7e99cabd65f","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":40,"quote":"7.3 Retriever Retrievers for handling tasks on reasoning and planning graphs are often modeled as graph traversers."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"d2068edc08df316d_c_5f45810b2e432322","docId":"d2068edc08df316d","docTitle":"Siren's Song in the AI Ocean: A Survey on Hallucination in Large Language Models","page":31,"quote":"Large dual encoders are generalizable retrievers."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_f3bfbf66a31a30d7","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":9,"quote":"BGM [26] keeps the retriever and LLM fixed,and trains a bridge Seq2Seq model in between."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_682f79d20bd7bb96","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":3,"quote":"We use a pre-trained bi-encoder from DPR to initialize our retriever and to build the document index."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_def28a5af43c8e23","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":7,"quote":"GenRead [13] replaces the retriever with an LLM generator, finding that LLM-generated contexts often contain more accurate answers due to better alignment with the pre-training objectives of causal language modeling."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_0129350a05e53f8f","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":40,"quote":"7.3 Retriever Retrievers for handling tasks on reasoning and planning graphs are often modeled as graph traversers."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_17e8bcc3c9b25731","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":49,"quote":"49 10.2 Retriever • Differentiating Neural and Symbolic Knowledge: Graph-structured data usually involves two distinct types of knowledge: symbolic-formatted knowledge, such as relations in knowledge graphs, and neural-formatted knowledge,"},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_4abe8a79f49843e3","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":10,"quote":"Fine-tuning of LLM can also be coordinated with fine-tuning of the retriever to align pref- erences."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031_c_29b186ec94bf67ad","docId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031","docTitle":"2401.15884_Corrective_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":1,"quote":"Generator Accurate Documents Inaccurate Documents Generator Figure 1: The examples show that a low-quality retriever is prone to introducing a substantial amount of irrelevant information, impeding the generators from acquiring accurate"},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_cd1c2e14380bfb91","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":30,"quote":"The retriever can be roughly classified as heuristic-based retriever and deep learning-based retriever."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_8b2e6c5acfee6f6a","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":2,"quote":"We combine a pre-trained retriever (Query Encoder + Document Index) with a pre-trained seq2seq model (Generator) and ﬁne-tune end-to-end."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_9575a1b71371de3e","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":3,"quote":"2.4 Training We jointly train the retriever and generator components without any direct supervision on what document should be retrieved."},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031_c_976957df22b5c100","docId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031","docTitle":"2401.15884_Corrective_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":3,"quote":"The retriever R aims to retrieve the top-K documents D = {dr1, ..., drk} that are relevant to the input X from the corpus C."},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_3169c306dc4be0d2","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":2,"quote":"essential to equip the retriever with directional awareness."},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_27912289ef765b6f","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":50,"quote":"The question of how to equip the retriever with these adaptive thinking, reasoning, and planning abilities remains a big problem."},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_3025ebdcb9ebb485","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":19,"quote":"ustering techniques to construct a KG from a set of texts. 3.3 Retriever Real-world facts in KGs can provide grounded information for generative models, enhancing the reliability of the model output."},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_7335f0306ab8fa20","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":11,"quote":"olformer, for instance, di- vides its retrieval process into distinct steps where LLMs proactively use retrievers, apply Self-Ask techniques, and em- ploy few-shot prompts to initiate search queries."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_97a2c1929ff7918a","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":6,"quote":"We report QA results for HippoRAG, the strongest retrieval baselines, ColBERTv2 and IRCoT, as well as IRCoT using HippoRAG as a retriever in Table 4."},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_b4fed2f43e42c2c0","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":13,"quote":"The recall@10 scores on these datasets were 0.823, 0.663, and 0.818, respectively, indicating the effectiveness of the retriever across different knowledge graph con- texts."},{"id":"c28","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_605a79ff07f8f2b5","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":2,"quote":"Like T5 [51] or BART, RAG can be ﬁne-tuned on any seq2seq task, whereby both the generator and retriever are jointly learned."},{"id":"c29","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_f3bfbf66a31a30d7","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":9,"quote":"In this approach, the retriever module is directly substituted to gen- erate relevant documents according to a query."},{"id":"c30","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_39a5dda334fd31c5","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":2,"quote":"Further- more, the use of the Schema Retriever is shown to significantly and consistently improve EDC’s performance."},{"id":"c31","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_4ee341034574c945","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":14,"quote":"It is to be noted that, similar to other RAG-based methods, there is a chance that the retriever may retrieve irrelevant information."},{"id":"c32","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_072aeadc2066d596","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":19,"quote":"The collapse could be due to a less-explicit requirement for factual knowledge in some tasks, or the longer target sequences, which could result in less informative gradients for the retriever."},{"id":"c33","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_76f23bae7f5d5e8b","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":3,"quote":"Concretely, the top K documents are retrieved using the retriever, and the generator produces the output sequence probability for each document, which are then marginalized, pRAG-Sequence(y|x) ≈ X z∈top-k(p(·|x)) pη(z|x)pθ(y|x, z) = X"},{"id":"c34","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_821ce241fcd8fca8","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":2,"quote":"As shown in Figure 1, our models leverage two components: (i) a retriever pη(z|x) with parameters η that returns (top-K truncated) distributions over text passages given a query x and (ii) a generator pθ(yi|x, z, y1:i−1) parametrized 1Code"},{"id":"c35","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_821ce241fcd8fca8","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":2,"quote":"To train the retriever and generator end-to-end, we treat the retrieved document as a latent variable."},{"id":"c36","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_e6a806de0215bb8c","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":3,"quote":"2.2 Retriever: DPR The retrieval component pη(z|x) is based on DPR [26]."},{"id":"c37","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_e6a806de0215bb8c","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":3,"quote":"Concretely, the top K documents are retrieved using the retriever, and then the generator produces a distribution for the next output token for each document, before marginalizing, and repeating the process with the following output token,"},{"id":"c38","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_3f7fee483c85589e","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":2,"quote":"We propose a trained Schema Retriever that re- trieves schema components relevant to the input text, akin to retrieval-augmented generation (Lewis et al., 2020), which we find improves the generated triplets."},{"id":"c39","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_38b152c9607dfd2e","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":6,"quote":"44.7 61.2 75.6 65.6 79.0 53.7 66.4 IRCoT + Contriever 39.1 52.2 51.6 63.8 65.9 81.6 52.2 65.9 IRCoT + ColBERTv2 41.7 53.7 64.1 74.4 67.9 82.0 57.9 70.0 IRCoT + HippoRAG (Contriever) 43.9 56.6 75.3 93.4 65.8 82.3 61.7 77.4 IRCoT + HippoRAG"},{"id":"c40","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_1cef8689d67ef49b","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":1,"quote":"We introduce RAG models where the parametric memory is a pre-trained seq2seq model and the non-parametric memory is a dense vector index of Wikipedia, accessed with a pre-trained neural retriever."},{"id":"c41","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_8bc4eb1f120e5a9e","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":11,"quote":"Questions are all you need to train a dense passage retriever."},{"id":"c42","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_9155a1afbff2cd04","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":1,"quote":"However, unlike conventional RAG, where the retriever, generator, and external data sources can be uniformly designed in the neural-embedding space, the uniqueness of graph-structured data, such as diverse-formatted and domain-specific"},{"id":"c43","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_414678129b4943a9","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":5,"quote":"The chronicles of rag: The retriever, the chunk and the generator."},{"id":"c44","chunkId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031_c_29b186ec94bf67ad","docId":"975aa1fd3c1b6031","docTitle":"2401.15884_Corrective_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":1,"quote":"When Hamm's script was rewritten, … Retriever ✗ Hamm."},{"id":"c45","chunkId":"bd72eebf611df136_c_c6246d06107d1dab","docId":"bd72eebf611df136","docTitle":"2410.05779_LightRAG_Simple_and_Fast_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":3,"quote":"ii) Data Retriever ψ(·): The relevant documents are obtained by comparing the query against the indexed data, also denoted as “relev